{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335940-questgions-on-investigation-rules","id":1335940,"title":"Questgions on Investigation Rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-15T14:05:56-07:00","id":1335940,"title":"Questgions on Investigation Rules?","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">7 AM</span></span></span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Ideas what skills qualify for Investigative Aide?<br /> <br /> <br /> Examples of how to use them?<br /> <br /> Get Impression but don't see as much in words, that a investigation different parties can be gathering clues.<br /> <br /> Think that will work? <br /> <br /> Can Teamwork actions be used? </span><br /> </span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T14:26:54-07:00","id":1335944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1335940-questgions-on-investigation-rules#post1335940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas what skills qualify for Investigative Aide?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Skill can theoretically apply. Mental ones are the most obvious (the book points out that Science and Medicine as examples for CSI lab techs or medical examiners to be rolling instead of Investigation). Academics, Computers, and Occult would be relevant for obtaining Clues through research or datamining. Crafts would help for Clues that might deal in distinct manufacturing details or purposeful mechanical sabotage. Politics would be useful for Clues that are more social in nature; like finding out the power dynamics in an organization to identify likely suspects.<br /> <br /> But Weaponry or Firearms could be used to generate Clues based on knowledge of the weapons involved in a crime, while Streetwise might let you get Clues based on your knowledge of local gang territories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Get Impression but don't see as much in words, that a investigation different parties can be gathering clues. </div> </div> </div>There's nothing theoretically stopping the group from splitting up and doing different parts of the Investigation at once, generating Clues faster. The key is good communication so they don't retread the same clues, or confuse things by going in wildly different directions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Teamwork actions be used? </div> </div> </div>If the party sticks together? Sure. If they split up? No. So it's a trade off. Stick together and potentially have a killer roll to get a great Clue, or split up and be more likely to get more Clues at once, but not necessarily as high quality ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T08:18:46-07:00","id":1336044,"title":"","content":"Difference between what Streetwise and larceny would find?<br /> <br /> Streetwise is more &quot;Ask questions of gangs&quot; larceny more hands on...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T13:54:42-07:00","id":1336092,"title":"","content":"Larceny would help find clues related to things like noticing how a lock or security system was defeated, figuring out what sort of tools might have been used to open a safe, etc. <br /> <br /> If you've seen the movie Red Dragon, the fact that the Tooth Fairy brings bolt cutters to one of the crimes scenes when he didn't need them is a major clue that Graham notices, and would be something that could come from a Larceny based roll as it's an oddity based in breaking into the victims' home and pushes Graham to establish that one of the doors had be replaced with a heavier duty one. Since the earlier door could have been opened with bolt cutters, and the new one couldn't, it creates an important part of the timeline.<br /> <br /> In general, the Physical Skills are going to focus on tools of the trade or applications of them. Survival easily gives you knowledge of knot tying, so you might be able to generate a Clue from what kinds of knots a suspect has been using (like they seem to use maritime knots even in situations where there might be a better knots if you're not using big wet ropes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}